1
00:00:55,530 --> 00:00:57,530
How about some music?

2
00:00:57,530 --> 00:01:00,530
No, let's wait till Robbie gets back from the airport.

3
00:01:00,530 --> 00:01:02,530
Did she say why she had to leave today?

4
00:01:02,530 --> 00:01:04,530
She told Robbie that her flight tomorrow was canceled,

5
00:01:04,530 --> 00:01:06,530
so she had to take an earlier flight today.

6
00:01:06,530 --> 00:01:08,530
This is terrible.

7
00:01:08,530 --> 00:01:11,530
Well, that must be him.

8
00:01:11,530 --> 00:01:12,530
Why is he blowing his horn like that?

9
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:13,530
I don't know.

10
00:01:13,530 --> 00:01:14,530
Maybe he's angry.

11
00:01:14,530 --> 00:01:16,530
Do you think we should take down the decorations?

12
00:01:16,530 --> 00:01:17,530
They'll just make him sad.

13
00:01:17,530 --> 00:01:18,530
Too late now.

14
00:01:18,530 --> 00:01:19,530
We should have done it sooner.

15
00:01:19,530 --> 00:01:21,530
Oh, here he comes.

16
00:01:21,530 --> 00:01:23,530
Hi.

17
00:01:23,530 --> 00:01:24,530
How'd it go?

18
00:01:24,530 --> 00:01:27,530
OK, I guess.

19
00:01:27,530 --> 00:01:30,530
Especially when Alexandra gave me a surprise ...

20
00:01:30,530 --> 00:01:31,530
Yeah? What was it?

21
00:01:31,530 --> 00:01:32,530
This!

22
00:01:32,530 --> 00:01:35,530
Alexandra! Alexandra

23
00:01:35,530 --> 00:01:40,530
Hi! What happened?

24
00:01:40,530 --> 00:01:44,530
I called my parents from the airport.

25
00:01:44,530 --> 00:01:45,530
When I told them

26
00:01:45,530 --> 00:01:47,530
my friends were giving me a party,

27
00:01:47,530 --> 00:01:48,530
they insisted that I stay.

28
00:01:48,530 --> 00:01:51,530
So now I'm taking a flight on Monday instead.

29
00:01:51,530 --> 00:01:53,530
That's great! Terrific!

30
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:55,530
But how did you know the party was for you?

31
00:01:55,530 --> 00:01:57,530
Well, Robbie told me when he gave me this.

32
00:01:57,530 --> 00:02:00,530
Oh, it's so pretty!

33
00:02:00,530 --> 00:02:02,530
It's lovely, Robbie.

34
00:02:02,530 --> 00:02:03,530
All right!

35
00:02:03,530 --> 00:02:04,530
Now we can really start the party!

36
00:02:04,530 --> 00:02:06,530
No. Would you mind?

37
00:02:06,530 --> 00:02:07,530
I'd like to say something first.

38
00:02:07,530 --> 00:02:08,530
Hear, hear!

39
00:02:08,530 --> 00:02:12,530
I would just like to thank all of you,

40
00:02:12,530 --> 00:02:13,530
my friends,

41
00:02:13,530 --> 00:02:17,530
who have made my stay in the United States so wonderful.

42
00:02:17,530 --> 00:02:21,530
And to Robbie and the Stewart family

43
00:02:21,530 --> 00:02:22,530
for opening their home to me.

44
00:02:22,530 --> 00:02:25,530
We should thank you.

45
00:02:25,530 --> 00:02:26,530
You're a real friend!

46
00:02:26,530 --> 00:02:30,530
And I also have a little surprise for you, Robbie.

47
00:02:30,530 --> 00:02:33,530
A little going-away present.

48
00:02:33,530 --> 00:02:34,530
Thank you.

49
00:02:34,530 --> 00:02:35,530
Open it, please.

50
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:38,530
I think you might be amused.

51
00:02:38,530 --> 00:02:43,530
OK. I can't believe it!

52
00:02:43,530 --> 00:02:46,530
I guess we were thinking the same thought.

53
00:02:46,530 --> 00:02:48,530
You had it engraved!

54
00:02:48,530 --> 00:02:50,530
Read it, Robbie.

55
00:02:50,530 --> 00:02:54,530
"In friendship, always. Alexandra." “

56
00:02:54,530 --> 00:02:55,530
I knew we thought alike,

57
00:02:55,530 --> 00:02:56,530
but this is too much!

58
00:02:56,530 --> 00:02:58,530
Thank you.

59
00:02:58,530 --> 00:02:59,530
All right!

60
00:02:59,530 --> 00:03:01,530
Let's have some music!

61
00:03:01,530 --> 00:03:11,530
Miss Pappas? Pappas

62
00:03:11,530 --> 00:03:12,530
Mr. Stewart ... Stewart

63
00:03:12,530 --> 00:03:16,530
Mrs. Stewart, may I have this dance? Stewart

64
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:19,530
My pleasure, Doctor.
